.TH RUFUX 1 "September 2026" "Rufux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rufux \- bootable USB creator for Linux (Rufus port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rufux
\fIlist\fR [\-\-json] [\-\-allow\-fixed]
.br
.B rufux
\fIprobe\fR \fIFILE\fR [\-\-detail]
.br
.B rufux
\fIchecksum\fR \fIFILE\fR [\-\-algo md5|sha1|sha256|sha512]
.br
.B rufux
\fIwrite\fR \fISRC DST\fR [\-\-dry\-run|\-\-real] [\-\-verify] [\-\-allow\-fixed] [\-\-allow\-file] [\-\-yes]
.br
.B rufux
\fIpartition\fR \fIDST\fR \-\-scheme gpt|dos \-\-layout single|esp+main [\-\-real] [\-\-yes] ...
.br
.B rufux
\fIformat\fR \fIDST\fR \-\-fs vfat|fat16|ntfs|exfat|ext2|ext3|ext4|udf [\-\-label \fIL\fR] [\-\-real] [\-\-yes] ...
.br
.B rufux
\fIextract\fR \fISRC\fR \fIDEST_DIR\fR [\-\-dry\-run]
.br
.B rufux
\fIinstall\-boot\fR \fIDST\fR \-\-mbr bios|gpt [\-\-real] [\-\-yes] ...
.br
.B rufux
\fIpersist\fR \fIDIR\fR \-\-size \fIMB\fR [\-\-label \fIL\fR] [\-\-dry\-run]
.br
.B rufux
\fIbadblocks\fR \fIDST\fR [\-\-allow\-file] [\-\-write\-patterns 1..4 \-\-yes]
.br
.B rufux
\fImount\fR|\fIumount\fR \fIDEV\fR [\-\-dry\-run]
.br
.B rufux
\fIsecureboot\-status\fR
.br
.B rufux
\fIvalidate\-efi\fR \fIFILE\fR
.br
.B rufux
\fIsmart\fR \fIDEV\fR
.br
.B rufux
\fIcheck\-boot\fR \fIFILE.efi\fR|\fIDIR\fR
.br
.B rufux
\fIupdate\-check\fR
.br
.B rufux
\fIcreate\fR \fISRC\fR|\fInone\fR \fIDST\fR \-\-mode dd|extract|format|dos|windows [\-\-scheme \fIS\fR] [\-\-fs \fIF\fR] [\-\-persist\-mb \fIN\fR] [\-\-wue bypass,nro,privacy,all,none] [\-\-ignore\-smart] ...
.br
.B rufux
\fIdownload\-windows\fR [\-\-list|\-\-list\-langs] [\-\-version 11|10] [\-\-edition \fIN\fR] [\-\-lang \fINAME\fR] [\-\-arch x64|ARM64|x86] [\-\-out \fIDIR\fR] [\-\-url\-only]
.br
.B rufux
\fI\-\-gui\fR [\-\-theme system|dark|light]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rufux creates bootable USB drives on Linux. Destructive commands default to
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR planning; real block-device writes need \fB\-\-real \-\-yes\fR
and root (sudo/pkexec). The GUI itself always runs unprivileged and
asks for elevation per operation: pressing START spawns the worker as
root through pkexec (desktop password prompt, no terminal needed),
streaming its progress back into the window.
.SH NEW IN 2.0
.TP
.B smart DEV
Asks smartctl for the drive's health. A drive that reports itself as failing is refused by \fBcreate\fR unless \fB\-\-ignore\-smart\fR is given; drives that report nothing (most USB sticks) are never blocked.
.TP
.B check\-boot
Checks UEFI bootloaders against the Secure Boot revocation lists (DBX hashes and certificates, SBAT, boot manager security version). Exit status 4 when one is revoked. \fBcreate\fR runs the same check on what it copies and warns.
.TP
.B download\-windows
Downloads a Windows 11 or 10 ISO from Microsoft's download service, the same way Rufus's Fido script does. \fB\-\-list\fR shows versions and editions, \fB\-\-list\-langs\fR the languages. A partial download is resumed. Microsoft rate-limits by address.
.TP
.B Virtual disks
\fBwrite\fR and \fBcreate \-\-mode dd\fR expand VHDX, dynamic VHD, VMDK, QCOW2 and VDI images with qemu-img. Images that refer to other files are refused.
.TP
.B Windows media, MBR scheme
Also gets legacy BIOS boot code (GRUB 2 in the gap before the first partition, which starts bootmgr) for both FAT32 and NTFS. GPT drives boot on UEFI only.
.SH EXAMPLES
List removable drives:
.PP
.RS
rufux list
.RE
.PP
Write an image (dry\-run first, then real with verify):
.PP
.RS
rufux write linux.iso /dev/sdb --dry\-run
.br
sudo rufux write linux.iso /dev/sdb --real --verify --yes
.RE
.PP
UEFI file flow with auto-mount (Phase 3):
.PP
.RS
sudo rufux create linux.iso /dev/sdb --mode extract --scheme gpt --fs vfat --yes
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR udisksctl (1),
.BR sfdisk (8),
.BR mkfs.vfat (8)
